      "explanation": "\\(5+10=15\\).",
      "id": "evaluate-coefficients",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_h238_q4#evaluate-coefficients",
      "title": "Evaluate both coefficients"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_h238",
        "cnm_h237"
      ],
      "explanation": "The lower indices are consecutive, so Pascal's identity combines the two coefficients. For integers \\(1\\le k\\le n\\), it states \\(C(n,k-1)+C(n,k)=C(n+1,k)\\). Taking \\(n=5\\) and \\(k=2\\) gives\n\\[\nC(5,1)+C(5,2)=C(6,2)=\\frac{6\\cdot5}{2\\cdot1}=15.\n\\]\nThus the value is \\(15\\).",
      "id": "apply-pascal-identity",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_h238_q4#apply-pascal-identity",
      "title": "Combine adjacent coefficients"
    }
  ],
